/mjx-container>. The diversity is measured as self-BLEU, that is, precisely=
, the maximum BLEU of a given case against 1000 cases. Lower self-BLEU indi=
cates better diversity. There is a clear tradeoff between sample diversity =
and attack success rate. Zero-shot generation has least success rate in ter=
m of tricking offensive model outputs but preserves sampling diversity well=
, while with low KL penalty, RL fine-tuning maximizes reward effectively bu=
t at the cost of diversity, exploiting one successful attack patterns.</p>
